{
  "_note": "Second pass on the homepage 'Formulated with' bar, as a full in-place section replacement. Two faults measured on the live page at 1440px: (1) the grid cell is 250px with 16px item padding, so 218px was the real ceiling and ACETYL HEXAPEPTIDE-8 was clamped to it, rendering 20px tall against its neighbours' 27-29px; (2) the heading inherits h2/48px Fraunces and shouts over the wordmarks it introduces. NOTE the trap this file exists to work around: `custom_css` is a TOP-LEVEL key of a section, a sibling of `settings`, not a member of it. Sending it through patch-template.py's `setting_updates` writes it inside `settings`, where Shopify ignores it — the push succeeds, the logo_width changes land, and the CSS silently does not. Only a whole-section write puts it in the right place.",
